Patterns: SDD

Purpose:
  Define architecture patterns available for selection. Patterns are
  reusable solutions to common architectural problems. AI MUST select
  a pattern based on project requirements, constraints, and trade-offs —
  not by default or preference.

Owns: ./

Patterns:

  Monolith:
    name: Monolith
    description: Single deployable application
    complexity: Low
    scale_fit: L0-L1
    pros:
      - simple deployment
      - easy development
      - low operational cost
    cons:
      - scaling limitations
      - team coordination challenges
      - technology lock-in
    when_to_use:
      - small team
      - low traffic
      - simple domain
      - prototype/MVP
    when_to_avoid:
      - high traffic
      - multiple teams
      - complex domain
      - independent scaling needs

  ModularMonolith:
    name: Modular Monolith
    description: Single deployable application with internal module boundaries
    complexity: Medium
    scale_fit: L1-L3
    pros:
      - simple deployment
      - clear module boundaries
      - easier than microservices
      - can extract modules later
    cons:
      - still single deployable
      - module boundaries require discipline
      - scaling limited to whole app
    when_to_use:
      - medium team
      - medium traffic
      - clear domain boundaries
      - want microservice benefits without complexity
    when_to_avoid:
      - very high traffic
      - independent scaling requirements
      - multiple autonomous teams

  Microservices:
    name: Microservices
    description: Multiple independently deployable services
    complexity: High
    scale_fit: L3-L5
    pros:
      - independent scaling
      - independent deployment
      - technology diversity
      - team autonomy
    cons:
      - operational complexity
      - distributed system challenges
      - higher infrastructure cost
      - network latency
    when_to_use:
      - large team
      - high traffic
      - clear domain boundaries
      - independent scaling needs
      - organizational alignment
    when_to_avoid:
      - small team
      - low traffic
      - simple domain
      - insufficient DevOps maturity

  EventDriven:
    name: Event-Driven Architecture
    description: Components communicate via events
    complexity: Medium-High
    scale_fit: L2-L5
    pros:
      - loose coupling
      - scalability
      - async processing
      - audit trail
    cons:
      - eventual consistency
      - debugging complexity
      - event schema evolution
      - ordering challenges
    when_to_use:
      - async workflows
      - event sourcing needed
      - multiple consumers
      - audit requirements
    when_to_avoid:
      - simple CRUD
      - strong consistency required
      - low complexity domain

  CQRS:
    name: Command Query Responsibility Segregation
    description: Separate read and write models
    complexity: Medium-High
    scale_fit: L2-L5
    pros:
      - optimized read/write paths
      - scalability
      - security (read/write separation)
    cons:
      - complexity
      - eventual consistency
      - more code
    when_to_use:
      - high read/write ratio difference
      - scaling bottlenecks
      - complex domain
    when_to_avoid:
      - simple domain
      - low traffic
      - strong consistency required

  EventSourcing:
    name: Event Sourcing
    description: State derived from event stream
    complexity: High
    scale_fit: L3-L5
    pros:
      - complete audit trail
      - temporal queries
      - event replay
      - consistent state
    cons:
      - complexity
      - learning curve
      - event schema evolution
      - storage requirements
    when_to_use:
      - audit requirements
      - temporal queries needed
      - event replay needed
      - complex state transitions
    when_to_avoid:
      - simple CRUD
      - no audit requirements
      - small team

  Serverless:
    name: Serverless
    description: Function-as-a-Service, no server management
    complexity: Medium
    scale_fit: L1-L4
    pros:
      - no infrastructure management
      - automatic scaling
      - pay-per-use
      - fast deployment
    cons:
      - cold starts
      - vendor lock-in
      - debugging difficulty
      - cost unpredictability
    when_to_use:
      - variable traffic
      - event-driven workloads
      - small team
      - rapid prototyping
    when_to_avoid:
      - consistent high traffic
      - long-running processes
      - low latency requirements

  Hexagonal:
    name: Hexagonal Architecture
    description: Ports and adapters, domain-centric
    complexity: Medium
    scale_fit: L1-L3
    pros:
      - testability
      - domain focus
      - infrastructure independence
      - clean boundaries
    cons:
      - more abstraction
      - learning curve
      - over-engineering for simple apps
    when_to_use:
      - complex domain
      - multiple adapters needed
      - high testability requirements
    when_to_avoid:
      - simple CRUD
      - small team
      - tight deadlines

  CleanArchitecture:
    name: Clean Architecture
    description: Dependency rule, outer circles depend on inner
    complexity: Medium-High
    scale_fit: L2-L4
    pros:
      - testability
      - framework independence
      - clear dependency direction
    cons:
      - complexity
      - more files
      - over-engineering risk
    when_to_use:
      - complex business logic
      - long-lived systems
      - multiple interfaces
    when_to_avoid:
      - simple apps
      - small team
      - MVP

  Layered:
    name: Layered Architecture
    description: Traditional layered approach (UI, Business, Data)
    complexity: Low-Medium
    scale_fit: L0-L2
    pros:
      - familiar
      - simple
      - easy to understand
    cons:
      - can become messy
      - dependency direction violations
      - scaling limitations
    when_to_use:
      - simple applications
      - small teams
      - standard CRUD
    when_to_avoid:
      - complex domain
      - high scalability needs

Selection:
  AI MUST select architecture pattern based on:
    ProjectScale (L0-L5)
    Team size
    Domain complexity
    Traffic patterns
    Scaling requirements
    Deployment constraints
    Budget
    Team capability

  OverengineeringGate:
    AI MUST flag OVERENGINEERING when:
      pattern complexity > project scale justifies
      team size < pattern requires
      traffic < pattern requires
      budget < pattern requires

  UnderengineeringGate:
    AI MUST flag UNDERENGINEERING when:
      availability requirements > pattern provides
      security requirements > pattern provides
      traffic > pattern can handle
      compliance requirements > pattern supports

Navigation:
  Project: @project/project.sdd
  Levels: @levels.sdd
  Scaling: @scaling.sdd
  Data: @data.sdd
  Availability: @availability.sdd
  Observability: @observability.sdd
  Networking: @networking.sdd
  Deployment: @deployment.sdd
  ProjectArchitecture: @project/architecture/INDEX.sdd
  Decisions: @project/decisions/INDEX.sdd

State: +
  